║  Storage:       32 GB / 64 GB eMMC                                       ║
║                                                                          ║
║  Display: X00TD — 5.99" 2160×1080 IPS LCD, 450 nits, 60 Hz              ║
║           X01BD — 6.26" 2280×1080 IPS LCD, 450 nits, 60 Hz              ║
║           Both use similar BOE/Tianma IPS panels with comparable         ║
║           brightness curves and backlight ranges.                        ║
║                                                                          ║
║  Kernel:  4.19.x (PSI-based LMKD, no legacy minfree tuning)             ║
║  NFC:     NXP PN553 (X00TD) / absent on most X01BD SKUs                 ║
║  Fingerprint: Goodix CDFinger (rear-mounted, both devices)               ║
║  Vibrator: ERM motor (both devices)                                      ║
║  Color:   LiveDisplay via kernel PCC (not AOSP Night Display)            ║
║  SIM:     Dual nano-SIM (both devices)                                   ║
║                                                                          ║
║  MEMORY STRATEGY:                                                        ║
║    This overlay uses middle-ground values suitable for 3–6 GB.           ║
║    PSI-based LMKD adapts kill pressure dynamically per actual RAM.       ║
║    config_customizedMaxCachedProcesses = 32 works well across all        ║
║    three variants:                                                       ║
║      3 GB — tight but functional, PSI kills aggressively as needed       ║
║      4 GB — comfortable, most apps stay cached                           ║
║      6 GB — plenty of headroom, 32 is a soft floor not a ceiling         ║
║    extra_free_kbytes = 32 MB prevents direct reclaim stalls on eMMC      ║
║    regardless of total RAM.                                              ║
║                                                                          ║
║  DISPLAY STRATEGY:                                                       ║
║    Both panels share the same backlight IC range (0–255) and similar     ║
║    nit output. The auto-brightness curve is calibrated for ~450 nits     ║
║    peak which matches both devices. Minor panel-to-panel variation       ║
║    is handled by the user brightness adjustment gamma.                   ║
║                                                                          ║
║  NOTIFICATION STRATEGY:                                                  ║
║    AutoPowerModes disabled — prevents aggressive idle batching           ║
║    Doze pulse enabled — screen briefly wakes on notification             ║
║    Interactive mode decoupled from display — CPU stays responsive        ║
║    Proximity suspend disabled — no lost notifications in pocket          ║
║                                                                          ║
║  GPU / GRAPHICS:                                                         ║
║    Adreno 509 (SDM636) and Adreno 512 (SDM660) have identical           ║
║    feature sets for overlay purposes — neither supports wide color       ║
║    gamut, both support HW color transform via PCC.                       ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
-->

